Revision history for Red

{{$NEXT}}
    - Promote experimental features to stable: has-one, refreshable, is-handling
      (the flags in `use Red <...>` remain accepted as no-ops for compatibility)
    - fixes: track in-place mutations of Positional/Associative/Json columns
      (`.push`, item assignment, `:delete`, nested writes on inflated Json) as
      dirty on `.^save`, by comparing the current value against a deep-clone
      snapshot taken at build/clean-up time. `dirty-old-values` for such
      columns now stores a deep-clone instead of a live container reference.
    - compiler: add fallback warnings via :warn, $*RED-COMPILER-WARN and RED_COMPILER_WARN
    - performance: resolve query-plan types once and streamline fingerprint traversal
    - performance: hydrate rows in one pass while retaining defaults and prefetched relationships
    - performance: avoid failure creation when optional cache and report settings are absent
    - performance: use lightweight hydration metadata while preserving custom column behavior
    - performance: build model defaults directly without intermediate sequences and pairs
    - fixes: retain bound predicate parameters inside uncached CASE branches and cyclic hashes
    - compiler: preserve comparison operator coercions and casts in compiled queries
    - fixes: bypass query-plan caching for cyclic positional values without losing later bindings
    - fixes: preserve arithmetic grouping in string casts and SQLite JSON array paths
    - performance: avoid column allocations during model access and key checks
    - performance: use native candidate matching during row inflation
    - tests: cover repeated model access and add a model access benchmark
    - performance: update plan-cache recency in constant time on cache hits
    - performance: forward compiled query arguments without rebuilding their capture
    - performance: frame plan-key strings without general-purpose serialization
    - performance: replace literal name separators without regex matching
    - performance: stop encoding discarded plan keys while retaining fallback bindings
    - performance: create temporary projection query classes on first use
    - performance: install projection initializers directly and defer intermediate query classes
    - performance: reuse generic projection storage methods with private row state
    - performance: resolve hydration target types directly from column metadata
    - tests: verify projection class identity, constructor isolation and concurrent initialization
    - queries: return uncached builder results when plan-cache capacity is zero
    - compiler: persist symbolic scalar comparison AST prototypes in module precompilation
    - performance: build hydration column maps in one pass and stop member lookup early
    - queries: cache SQL plans without sharing cursors, connections or query results
    - compiler: reuse scalar comparison predicates with private captured parameters
    - compiler: keep the unsupported-template exception outside the GLOBAL stash
    - tests: verify plan reuse and add a query construction/execution benchmark
    - compiler: specialize direct Red::AST factories and validators during CHECK
    - compiler: reuse capture-free templates without sharing captured values between queries
    - compiler: compile membership predicates and preserve word-list quoting semantics
    - compiler: translate map assignments, compound assignments, increments, and JSON deletion
    - compiler: buffer update effects and compile sequential statements and scalar locals
    - compiler: bind row-independent constructors and function calls as runtime captures
    - compiler: recognize primed Whatever callbacks, booleans, Hash colonpairs, and lists
    - compiler: support dynamic JSON indexes and existence without dropping index adverbs
    - compiler: preserve mutation fallback and safely reject compound-assignment metaoperators
    - compiler: report translation decisions and test actual template evaluation
    - compiler: add opt-in CHECK-time RakuAST templates for map, grep, first, and sort
    - tests: cover compiled queries and native dispatch with a dedicated RakuAST CI job
    - schema: add named CHECK and PostgreSQL EXCLUDE constraints with driver selection
    - indexes: support access methods, per-key operator classes and partial predicates
    - pg: add range constructors and native range/regex expression helpers
    - catalogs: compare index methods, operator classes and predicates before reusing indexes

0.2.7  2026-10-18T05:55:59+01:00
    - relationships: support .^create on empty scalar relationships with automatic foreign keys (#475)
    - relationships: resolve string/type models consistently and isolate creation contexts per source
    - queries: keep aggregate projection models isolated during concurrent query construction (#554)
    - transactions: warn when guard.do returns a pending Promise without retaining its work
    - transactions: add guard.do/start with callbacks and automatically release manual blocks
    - transactions: add retain/release participants with rollback on the last release
    - transactions: add explicit :$guard commit/rollback control, including asynchronous scopes
    - transactions: reject closed scopes and overlapping access, and clean up active cursors
    - transactions: use savepoints for nested red-do transactions on the same connection
    - schema: declare named, composite and expression indexes with indexed/index/unique-index traits
    - schema: support unique expressions and add declared indexes to existing tables with ^create-indexes
    - sqlite/pg: inspect existing indexes and preserve legacy unique constraints
    - queries: translate Cartesian products of ResultSeqs and finite value collections to SQL
    - queries: preserve tuple shapes, model instances, ordering, and pagination in products

0.2.6  2026-10-15T18:34:50+01:00
    - tests: preserve multiplicity in unordered results and use portable CTE fixtures
    - pg: store Rat columns as numeric to preserve rational key comparisons
    - pg: fix date-part extraction and recognize date/datetime cast result types
    - queries: execute tail and reverse in SQL, preserving pagination and ordering
    - queries: retain primary-key ordering through scalar and container projections
    - queries: count scalars and NULL as one element, preserving absent JSON paths
    - queries: support argumentless sort for scalar projections
    - queries: chain scalar, Hash, Array, and List projections through map/grep/sort
    - queries: fuse safe map/grep/sort stages and retain necessary SELECT boundaries
    - queries: preserve ordering, converters, correlated aliases, and statement binds
    - tests(queries): cover lazy execution and projection chains in SQLite and Pg
    - json: bind paths, support dynamic keys/indexes, and preserve scalar JSON types
    - json: compose updates to the same column and evaluate Pg arithmetic in SQL
    - json: add existence, array deletion, member counts, and recursive containment
    - json: distinguish JSON null from SQL NULL and report serialization errors
    - tests(json): cover SQLite and Pg operations, including special keys and nested paths

0.2.5  2026-08-23T18:10:25+01:00
    - .perl -> .raku
    - pg: translate .index to STRPOS() with proper binding (aligns .index/.contains on Postgres)
    - tests(pg): make t/82–t/85 Pg-safe and idempotent
      - t/82: Company.id marked as primary key to satisfy Pg FK
      - t/83/t/84: schema(...).drop.create to avoid DDL collisions
      - t/85: drop/create C to ensure correct columns for string funcs
    - ci(pg): add PostgreSQL job to GitHub Actions; run t/ suite against Pg
    - pg(json): stringify-json; #> (path), #- (remove), and jsonb_set updates with to_jsonb/::jsonb binding
    - pg: map MINUS to EXCEPT; use $n placeholders for parameters
    - sql(binding): route AST::Value through wildcard-value; fix INSERT binding to use deflated values
    - implement prefetch

